1. **JUSTIFICATION GAP — the CS-drain estimate loses the residue-degree factor \(d\).**

Quoted target from R1.1:

> “\(u_{\mu,d}(M)/Q^{\mu(M-1)} \le K M^B Q^{-(M-c)}\),”  
> with \(Q=q^d\).

But ANNEX-LEMMA GENIND-C2 concludes only:

> “CS-drain part … \(\le K_c N^{B_c} q^{-(N-c_c)}\).”

For \(d>1\), this is strictly weaker than the required
\[
Q^{-(N-c)}=q^{-d(N-c)}.
\]
No \(N\)-independent constant converts \(q^{-N}\) into \(q^{-dN}\). The preceding calculation retains \(d\),
\[
|K|^{-M^\star}\le q^{-e d\deg(\psi)(N-1-H)+O(1)},
\]
but the final height summation drops it without deriving the needed \(q^{-dN}\) bound. Thus C2, as displayed, does not supply the full \((A2\text{-RATE})\) member subsequently consumed by C1.

Concrete failure scenario: take \(d=2\), \(Q=q^2\), and a hypothetical CS-child drain fraction \(q^{-3M/2}\). It satisfies C2’s stated \(O(q^{-M})\) conclusion but violates every \(O(\mathrm{poly}(M)Q^{-M})=O(\mathrm{poly}(M)q^{-2M})\) bound. In C1’s growing-window regime, multiplying by the route factor \(Q^{-D}=q^{-2D}\) then gives \(q^{-2N+M/2}\), not the claimed \(Q^{-N}\)-scale decay. The stronger conclusion may follow after retaining \(d\) throughout, but the written argument does not establish it.

This route is disjoint from the prior reports’ \(d=1\) GENH4 window/slope analysis.

